From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:03:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 089/148] hjviewer: one notice box, HjvCallout, in soft tones
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UX-S1 (U49): the app's notices are one widget. HjvCallout(text, tone,
icon, title, actions, onClose, stacked, onCanvas, titleOneLine) in
common/hjv_style.dart, exported by common/widgets/dialog.dart next to
hjvNoteBlock, which is now its neutral tone (its warning one with
`warning`), with the same signature. The look: radius md, 12 inside, an
18 px icon 8 before the text, the title 13/600, the text 13/1.45 in the
secondary colour (danger's in the text colour), the actions at the right
of a text of one line and below it otherwise, an 18 px close x with a 32 px
target on a desktop and 48 on a phone. `stacked` puts the actions at the
box's width, each at least 34 high (the 200 px pane); `onCanvas` draws a
card with a border; high contrast adds a border. HjvCallout.rich takes a
widget in the text's place (a tooltip, a selectable text).

HjvPalette has the soft tones and their text colours (successSoft/Text,
warningSoft/Text, dangerSoft with dangerText, infoSoft/infoText as the
accent's), 4.5:1 for every text on them; the icons and actions take the
tone's text colour. hjvTint stays for the peer tiles and avatars.

Moved onto it: P1 (warning, stacked, its title on one line), P2 and P3's
home line (success, stacked), G2 (neutral card, stacked, U05's pane form),
G1 (info), G3 (neutral, a card on a phone, as high with its [로그인] as
without), the device list's banner (danger with [다시 시도], or neutral),
buildErrorBanner (danger, its translated text in a Text of three lines at
most and whole in its tooltip, [다시 시도], the close x), the update strip
(info, one action and the close x). The install page puts G1 first and the
licence below as a caption of one line with its link; its buttons have no
icons, [수락하고 설치] last.

Tests: hjviewer_style_test.dart, the tones' contrast in both themes and
the callout's widget tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
